# Branch context visibility

Single-branch tenants should never see branch names like "Main Branch" in admin UI.

## Rule

Use `shouldShowBranchContext()` from `@/lib/branch-selector-visibility` (or `branchSelector.showBranchContext` from `getPageBranchSelectorProps()`) before rendering:

- `BranchSelector`
- Static branch labels/cards ("Branch", "Main Branch", etc.)
- Page descriptions that append a branch name

When `showBranchContext` is `false`, render nothing — do not fall back to a read-only branch name card.

## Helpers

- `BranchSelector` already returns `null` when context is hidden.
- For copy, use `appendBranchContext(description, branchName, showBranchContext)`.
- Prefer passing `showBranchContext` from server-side `getPageBranchSelectorProps()` rather than re-deriving in client components.

## Examples

```tsx
// Good — selector only when multi-branch
{branchSelector.showBranchContext ? <BranchSelector {...branchSelector} /> : null}

// Bad — fallback branch name for single-branch tenants
{showBranchSelector ? <BranchSelector /> : <p>{branchName}</p>}

// Good — generic description when branch context is hidden
appendBranchContext("Compose and print A4 documents", branchName, showBranchContext)
```

Reference: `src/features/attendance/components/timekeeping-calendar-page-content.tsx`, `src/app/(dashboard)/pos/page.tsx`
